 names←PropList resolveAliases names;lc;lcpl;i;n;obj
⍝ Map legacy ⎕WC property names onto the modern names in PropList.
⍝
⍝ Native ⎕WC still honours several spellings that no longer appear in any
⍝ PropList, because the properties were renamed long after applications had
⍝ started using them:
⍝
⍝   Bitmap -> Picture      verified against Dyalog 20.0: ⎕WC'Image' pts
⍝                          ('Bitmap' 'BM') leaves ⎕WG'Picture' as 'BM'.
⍝   Font   -> FontObj      the "object property" family -- a bare name was
⍝   Cursor -> CursorObj    superseded by <name>Obj and the old spelling still
⍝   Icon   -> IconObj      works. See objProps for the full set.
⍝
⍝ Applications predating those renames -- which is most of the ⎕WC code anyone
⍝ wants to move to the browser -- depend on this. Without it the property is
⍝ passed through under its old name and the client silently ignores it, which
⍝ presents as "nothing renders" rather than as an error.
⍝
⍝ The <name>Obj rule is derived from PropList rather than hard-coded, so it
⍝ holds for every class with no table to keep in step. A name is only rewritten
⍝ when the class has the Obj form AND lacks the bare form: Form and Static have
⍝ both Hint and HintObj, and there 'Hint' must stay 'Hint'.
 lcpl←⎕C PropList
 :For i :In ⍳≢names
     lc←⎕C n←i⊃names
     :If (⊂lc)∊lcpl
         :Continue                    ⍝ already a property of this class
     :EndIf
     :If (lc≡'bitmap')∧(⊂'picture')∊lcpl
         (i⊃names)←(lcpl⍳⊂'picture')⊃PropList
     :ElseIf (⊂obj←lc,'obj')∊lcpl
         (i⊃names)←(lcpl⍳⊂obj)⊃PropList
     :EndIf
 :EndFor
